  "scenario": {
    "id": "synthetic-switchback-review-2026-11-01",
    "contextWarnings": [
      "SYNTHETIC TRAINING ONLY. This project uses the built-in mathematical demo hillside and invented road, stream, harvest, review-area and D-line features. It contains no survey, LiDAR or site data and has no real-world vertical datum.",
      "Switchback starter assumptions: two 90-degree circular arcs, each radius 40 m; approach 50 m; connecting straight 10 m; departure 80 m; constant extension grade +3%. Added length is 265.663706 m and parallel-leg separation is 90 m. These are geometric examples, not a road class or BC design standard.",
      "The baseline is the original demo hillside access road. The left and right alternatives preserve that route then add their return bend. Their endpoints differ, so they are not equivalent access solutions; compare geometry and quantities for training only.",
      "Formation elevation is continuous at the original road end. The extension changes the tangent grade to +3% without adding a vertical curve at the join. Review the profile, grades and vertical controls before treating any edited layout as a proposed design.",
      "Template assumptions are 3 m formation width each side, 3% normal crossfall, 0.75H:1V cut slope, 1.5H:1V fill slope, 1 m ditch width, 0.5 m ditch depth and 0.25 m surface depth. The demo turnout and terminal landing remain at their original stations. No vehicle-widening or superelevation criteria are entered.",
      "Sampling is 5 m along the road plus exact event stations, with a 35 m cross-section half-width. Terrain resolution metadata is synthetic, not measured accuracy. Training unit rates, reusable-cut factor and review thresholds are assumptions, not quotations or approved design limits.",
      "Curve review is a geometric screen. It does not verify an articulated truck swept path, whole-switchback widening, leg or batter clearance, slope stability, drainage design, or curvature-corrected earthwork quantities. No terrain source file or online terrain request is needed to reopen this demo."
    ],
    "terrainCoveragePercent": 100
  },
